LAND_RESET_JUDGES_PER_MIN = 2
LAND_RESET_STAGGER_S = 3600.0
# The host's pace of judgments (LandQueue.window_room): each judgment is charged LAND_JUDGE_COST of each pool, and the
# pace comes from GitHub's own live count of the login (the land queue's reading: /rate_limit, free): what is left over
# the pool's hard reserve (hard_reserve_floor), spread evenly over the time to its reset. A judgment starts when the
# last one charged to that pool is at least cost / pace ago, and none starts while what is left is under one judgment's
# cost. So the spend follows the login's real state, never a fixed share: the share this replaced (land.json
# "windowShare", else 0.05 GraphQL and 0.10 REST of a fixed 5000 an hour, ramped over 10 min) held 54 of 72 waiting
# lands on huge-blue at 2026-11-21 20:05Z "not judged this window: host cap (graphql)" with 1107 GraphQL points left on
# the login. With no fresh reading (a lane-gh broker client, a refused /rate_limit) a pool is unpaced: the login's
# latch, the queue park and the shim's own refusal are what is measured there. An entry the pace leaves out keeps its
# place (judge_order) and says so (land_line: "not judged this window: host cap"). Measured
# on the broker client gcp-agent-lane-1 from gh-quota's calls.jsonl: one judgment sent about 5 calls, 2-3 of them
# GraphQL-shaped (`pr view`, `api graphql`; 01:38-01:48Z 2026-11-20: 116 over ~23 judgments, 44 GraphQL; 22:38-22:50Z
# 2026-11-19: 517 over ~63, 217 GraphQL), and the queue sent 135 calls in the ten minutes after the 01:38Z reset with
# 31 entries waiting. GraphQL is the pool that runs out on a lane VM (the broker's read Apps answer REST gets only).
# A judgment the cap leaves out only for GraphQL (REST still fits, or is uncapped) is not skipped: it is judged from this
# host's caches (`land_judge explain --cache-only LAND_CACHE_ONLY_MAX_AGE`), which sends nothing to GitHub and is
# charged nothing. A webview verdict glaeda-gh's checks cache holds in run order, the daemon's rollup snapshot and the
# gh shim's kept answers judge it; an "ok" there is advisory and the merge it names is judged live by the shim, as any
